HanClinto <HanClinto@gmail.com> writes:

> Lately I've been playing pacifists. For me, doing Sokobon is usually
> pretty dangerous, as I often don't have a magic whistle for pets, and
> if a monster is trapped behind a boulder, it's a royal pain to clear

It is often easier to avoid trapping monsters behind boulders than to
solve the situation without getting luck penalty.
The problematic place where monsters can get trapped is usually the long
corridor that contains the row of holes to be filled, when most of them
are already filled.
Just go around the boulder and take a look at the corridor before you push
the boulder beyond the last square where you can walk around it. If there
are any monsters, kill them (or otherwise get them out of the way if they
are peacefuls you don't want to kill) before pushing the boulder there.

True, monsters CAN still get created to the remaining part of the corridor
after that, but MOSTLY this procedure helps.

